(2) The responsibility of the City Government in efforts to Protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

Article 4

The scope of regulation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection includes:

a. protection of women;

b. protection of Children;

c. fulfillment of Children's rights;

d. improvement of quality of life of women and children;

e. community participation; and

f. guidance, supervision, assistance.

g. gender and child data system, disaggregated data on women and children;

Article 2

The implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection is based on the principles of:

a. best interests of women and Children;

b. gender justice and gender equality;

c. local wisdom;

d. law enforcement and legal certainty.

e. non-discrimination;

f. right to life, survival, and development;

g. respect for the opinion of Children; and

h. law enforcement and legal certainty.

Article 9

The City Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Working Group as referred to in Article 8 has the duties of:

a. promoting and facilitating Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to each Regional Apparatus;

b. conducting socialization and advocacy of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to sub-district heads, Village Heads and Village Chiefs;

c. preparing work programs every year;

d. encouraging the realization of planning and budgeting that is Responsive to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

e. preparing the work plan of the Women's Empowerment and Child Protection working group every year;

f. being accountable to the Mayor through the Deputy Mayor;

g. formulating policy recommendations to the Mayor;

h. preparing the profile of Regional Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

i. monitoring the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in each agency;

j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;

k. preparing the City Women's Empowerment and Child Protection regional action plan; and

I. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of Focal Points in each Regional Apparatus.

Part Six

Enhancement of the Role, Quality, and Capability of Women in the Social Sector

Article 14

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social sector include:

a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential;

b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women;

c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;

d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;

e. facilitating and endeavoring the preservation of customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;

f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge regarding independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;

g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; and

h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the City.

Article 39

Provision of services for families as referred to in Article 34 paragraph (1) letter b includes:

a. communication, information and education;

b. contraceptive devices and medicines;

c. recording and reporting of family planning services;

d. adequate health service facilities and infrastructure; and

e. lactation rooms in every public facility.

CHAPTER VI CHILD PROTECTION

Article 64

The City Government, in order to provide protection to Children:

a. implements and supports national policies in the implementation of Child Protection in the City;

b. guarantees Children to exercise their rights in expressing opinions in accordance with the age and intelligence level of Children;

c. conducts prevention of Violence against Children by optimizing the role of customary institutions;

d. conducts socialization, seminars and counseling regarding Child Protection and rights;

e. develops child-friendly school models;

f. provides public facilities that are friendly and safe for Children; and

g. encourages public awareness of the importance of Protection for Children.

CHAPTER VIII GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 70

(1) The City Government is obliged to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of Women's empowerment and protection of Child victims of Violence.

(2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:

a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;

b. technical guidance and training;

c. provision of facilities;

d. monitoring; and

e. evaluation.

(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is in order to realize the objectives of empowerment and Protection of women and Child victims of Violence in accordance with minimum service standards.

